#Type Name       ID  GECOS                         Home directory
u     raspisump  -   "Raspi-Sump system user"      /var/lib/raspi-sump

# Supplementary group (idempotent - systemd-sysusers does nothing if the
# user is already a member). gpio is not guaranteed to exist on every
# system; unlike a plain `usermod`, this line creates it if missing rather
# than silently skipping - harmless if no udev rule assigns GPIO device
# nodes to it, and correct if one does.
m     raspisump  gpio

# Deliberately NOT in systemd-journal: that grants read access to the
# entire system journal (auth logs, other services, kernel messages, all
# of it), not just raspisump's own two units. raspisump runs a network-
# facing web app - too broad a grant for what it buys. web/system.py's
# get_journal_log() and cli.py's rsumpsupport journalctl calls already
# handle the no-access case gracefully (empty result / error string
# embedded in the support bundle), so the admin "System Status" log tail
# and support bundle just show nothing for those lines instead.

# nginx on Arch runs as 'http' (Debian: 'www-data') - add it to
# raspisump's group so it can reach the Flask unix socket at
# /run/raspi-sump/flask.sock (mode 0750, owned by raspisump:raspisump).
m     http       raspisump
